-- title:
--   Non-emptiness of the finite Igusa chart over O
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N₀, q$ with $N₀ \neq 0$ and $q$ prime, and assume $q \nmid N₀$ (hypothesis `hqN`). Let $\mathfrak{P}$ be a term of the structure `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, i.e. a bundle of data and properties for the Igusa-type model `DRLevel.X N₀ q` together with its structure morphism `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring `DRLevel.R q` (the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $q$); among its fields are properness, flatness, integrality, normality on affine opens, a curve model `Meta` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with an isomorphism `eeta` onto the base change, compatibility with the Galois action, a non-emptiness field for the chart over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a pinning of the chart algebra by $q$-expansions, generic smoothness of relative dimension $1$ and geometric integrality, and sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$ over the base. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $q$ (hypothesis `hϖO`), and let $\rho_O : \mathtt{DRLevel.R}\ q \to O$ be a ring homomorphism. The conclusion asserts that the open subscheme of the fibre product $\mathtt{X}\ N₀\ q \times_{\operatorname{Spec} \mathtt{R}\ q} \operatorname{Spec} O$ obtained as the preimage, under the first projection, of the open image of the top open under `IgusaScheme.ιFin (N₀ * q) q` has a point, i.e. its underlying type is `Nonempty`.
--
--   This is the non-emptiness statement for the finite ($j \neq \infty$) Igusa chart of the model after base change along $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$; it is the instance under which germs over that open, and hence chart coordinates, may be formed. It is used in the analysis of the node coordinates and of the widths of the components of the special fibre in terms of the place specialisation.
-- source:
